Compliance with ESG Standards
Each Shareholder acknowledges and supports the Company’s aim to align its operations with recognized ESG standards (e.g., the UN Global Compact, the OECD Guidelines for Multinational Enterprises, or other comparable frameworks), and shall cooperate with the Company’s efforts to meet or exceed such benchmarks.


Mission and Purpose
The Shareholders acknowledge and support the Company’s commitment to operating in a sustainable and responsible manner, promoting a positive environmental and social impact and creating long-term economic value[, in line with the agreed theory of change].


Company Values
The Shareholders acknowledge that the Company’s purpose and mission[, as specified in the Articles of Association and further documented by the Board in its theory of change] (the Mission), shall be supported by (i) responsible business practices, (ii) the creation of long term value for relevant stakeholders and (iii) a transition to sustainable economic activities, in line with accepted environmental, social and governance (ESG) principles (collectively, the Company Values).


Theory of Change
a) [Within 6 months of the closing of the investment/As soon as practicable], the Board shall develop and formally adopt and keep updated [or cause the shareholders to adopt] a Theory of Change (the ToC) for the Company, which shall (i) align with the Company’s [Mission/Purpose/Values] and (ii) outline the specific outcomes, impact pathways, and short-, mid-, and long-term objectives the Company seeks to achieve, including measurable ESG and sustainable goals.
b) The Board shall further oversee the integration of the ToC into the Company’s business operations, strategic planning, and performance metrics and provide its best efforts to ensure the ToC remains an integral component of the Company’s strategic direction.
c) The Board shall identify, approve and periodically review key ESG and sustainable indicators to measure progress under the ToC.


